// The LOCAL-declaration half of the same rule as `export_qualified_ref`. A qualified spelling reaches no
// further than an `import` would, and that has to hold in every position that NAMES a type — a field, a
// parameter, a return type and, here, a local variable declaration:
//
//     std::collections::BTreeNode<int32, int32> n = …;   // ACCEPTED, before this rule
//
// `lib/std/collections/sorted_map.kama` says `export { SortedMap };` — the B-tree node is the map's
// internal structure. A local is scope-bound, so this position never escaped anything on its own; the
// reason to close it is that a half-enforced rule is worse to inherit than an unenforced one. What is
// still NOT checked is an expression that never names the type, which is not a declaration at all and
// belongs to expression type checking.
import { std::collections::SortedMap };

fn int32 depth() {
    slot std::collections::BTreeNode<int32, int32> n;
    return 0;
}

fn int32 main() { return 0; }
